  "problem": "Publisher dictionaries and payload names can differ while historical extraction currently combines or replays fields through legacy shapes. PR-008 needs an additive identity boundary that preserves exact names, semantics and provenance without treating counts or punctuation as proof of equivalence.",
  "resulting_behavior": "The v1.2 variable identity schema and package functions preserve literal wire names, labels, concepts, definitions, source and observed type assertions, units/applicability, literal code values, missingness, explicit mapping states and capture pointers. CDC/Census/CMS versioned adapters are replayable from capture hashes and JSON pointers. Existing cdc_columns/census_variables transformations and frozen machine contracts remain unchanged. Publication and promotion remain false; unresolved context and HCRIS discrepancies cannot mint or select a resolved identity.",
